add('S3-status-launch', 'E4-S3', 'Status projection and app/serve launch ownership', [
  'src/cli/runtime/status.ts', 'src/shared/cli-app-status-projection.ts', 'src/shared/runtime-host-connection-state.ts', 'src/cli/runtime/launch.ts'
], [
  'Local status with absent/invalid bootstrap returns synthetic local-status ok:true, appfalse/pidnull and runtime not_running or stale_bootstrap, reachablefalse/runtimeIdnull. Valid bootstrap probes status.get for1000ms. Successful response projects ready versus graph_not_ready, connection state, optional appVersion/capabilities/degradations and app pid from bootstrap.',
  'Any status-probe exception falls back to process.kill(pid,0) if positive pid. Any kill exception, including permission denial, is treated false by historical source; true=>starting, false=>stale_bootstrap. This is NOT evidence of exited. Root must reconcile this source behavior with required live/unverifiable/exited semantics rather than silently port an unsafe exit inference.',
  'Remote app projection has pidnull and running only when desktopWindowStatus available; legacy positive authoritativeWindowId implies available. Runtime connection state prioritizes missing entry checking, reconnecting, absent-status transport state, closed/disconnected, nonready/checking, workspace-window-closed, connected. Connected overall includes runtime-unavailable/window-closed; these refer to transport, not graph/desktop readiness.',
  'openOrca returns remote status without launching locally. Local blocked status rejects before launch; otherwise launch is attempted even for available desktop, then available returns immediately. Poll every250ms until available, reject blocked immediately, timeout15s default reports runtime_open_timeout and possible headless runtime.',
  'launchOrcaApp prefers nonblank ORCA_OPEN_COMMAND through shell, then ORCA_APP_EXECUTABLE, then ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE packaged executable (Mac .app via open when detectable); strips ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for executable launches. Detached launch ignores asynchronous errors, unrefs and leaves openOrca to observe readiness. Missing launcher yields runtime_open_failed.',
  'serve builds --serve plus truthy port/address and boolean JSON/pairing flags; recipe-json requires projectRoot. Recipe mode detaches with stdin ignored/stdout pipe/stderr inherited; ordinary serve inherits stdio or adds IPC for Mac update handoff. cwd is app root. Existing install-requested handoff resumes supervisor; otherwise spawn and supervise.',
  'Recipe readiness waits60s, decodes streaming UTF-8, accepts only valid orca-server recipe JSON line, emits sanitized fixed stderr notice for nonrecipe output, writes first valid trimmed result, destroys pipe/unrefs/returns0. Timeout rejects runtime_serve_failed and SIGTERMs child; close flushes tail then rejects if no valid result. Ordinary serve supervisor/update-install internals remain separate.',
  'Executable app-root flag enabled only env==1. Extracted Linux AppImage with adjacent AppRun disables sandbox for root or failed/timed-out2s unshare -Ur true probe. Windows .cmd/.bat executable uses shell:true here; this launch path does not call the stricter Windows token wrapper.'
], ['Port runtime-client.test.ts and launch/serve supervisor suites with mocked spawn and disposable fixture executables; do not open real user windows.', 'Add status malformed bootstrap/auth/RPC failure/EPERM/ESRCH fixtures; assert unreachable remains unverifiable in rewrite liveness contracts and require root decision for source discrepancy.', 'Test Mac bundle/open and interrupted update handoff, Linux AppImage root/unshare outcomes, Windows batch launch, valid/invalid/SSH recipe stdout, split UTF-8/CRLF/final no-newline, error/close/timeout races and child ownership after successful readiness.'], ['runtime-workspace-window-availability helper, Mac bundle discovery, serve-update-supervisor/install handoff implementation and child-process runProcessSync are not fully reviewed here; E5/platform and runtime owners must link accepted evidence or retain open.']);

add('S4-keychain', 'E4-S4', 'Claude macOS Keychain effects', ['src/main/claude-accounts/keychain.ts'], [
  'Owner is process host/current OS user, not selected remote runtime; non-darwin reads returnnull and writes/deletes do nothing. Read scoped raw/canonical-realpath services before unsuffixed legacy; strict scoped read never tries legacy. Missing realpath preserves raw alias.',
  'Scoped service is Claude Code-credentials plus first8 SHA256 hex of NFC configDir; managed service is Orca Claude Code Managed Credentials keyed by accountId. USER then USERNAME then userInfo username; anything outside ASCII alphanumeric dot underscore hyphen, or lookup failure, maps claude-code-user. Cleanup additionally tries raw env username if different.',
  'Reads execute security find-generic-password and trim returned stdout; blank successful output throws. Not-found code44 or message/stderr containing could not be found/not be found =>null; other failures propagate. Ordinary writes update named service via add-generic-password -U. Runtime writes scoped first then unsuffixed legacy, so second-write failure can leave partial effects.',
  'Ordinary delete tries scoped aliases plus legacy and ignores every deletion failure; strict delete tries only scoped aliases and ignores only not-found. Both iterate cleanup users. Managed deletion is ordinary ignore-failure.',
  'Every security command has execFile timeout3000 plus independent3000ms settlement timer; stalled callback kills child then rejects ETIMEDOUT with empty stderr. Callback errors retain stdout/stderr; completion/timeout guarded once. No rollback across multiple writes/deletes.'
], ['Port keychain.test.ts with execFile mock; add realpath/NFC aliases, strict missing versus denied, blank successful read, Linux/Windows no-op, synchronous spawn throw, late callback after timer, managed service and partial dual-write failure.', 'Only after source acceptance, run disposable macOS Keychain namespace integration fixtures under explicit test credentials; never real Claude accounts. Existing mocked tests do not prove keychain permission behavior.']);

