  'Ownership: caller formats already-returned records; a displayed host/profile/path is not a fresh host observation. These helpers return strings without setting an exit code or printing. S1 printResult call sites select text versus JSON.',
  'Browser snapshot prints page id, title/em-dash/URL and raw snapshot; screenshot prints decoded base64 byte count, using Buffer.byteLength(base64) and a floor(length*3/4) catch fallback. Tab rows mark active with *, optionally show profile label ?? id ?? Unknown, and return the explicit empty-list message. Profile rows mark default, use browserFamily ?? none and emit ua:native only for native mode. Show/clone use unknown/default fallback identities; empty strings survive nullish fallbacks.',
