  'printResult at format.ts:74 prints pretty JSON (indent2) to stdout after computer screenshot preprocessing, otherwise formatter(result) to stdout. reportCliError at137 prints JSON to stdout or formatCliError string to stderr. formatCliError itself only returns a string. No helper here sets process.exitCode; S1 entrypoint/handler owns exit behavior. Formatter/serialization exceptions are not caught here.',
  'Text error precedence: RuntimeClientError runtime_unavailable returns original message if data.orchestrationRequestId is any string, otherwise appends Orca-not-running hint; this occurs before conflict and nextSteps handling. Then recognized automation conflict wins, then RuntimeClientError string-only nextSteps, then computer invalid_argument fallback. RpcFailure subclasses ClientError so later subtype branches may already be shadowed. Non-Error becomes String(error).',
  'JSON RPC failure preserves response, except classified conflict restores code, strips trailing code token and uses existing nonnullish data or recovery. Non-RPC failure synthesizes id local, ok false, _meta.runtimeId null, code conflict ?? ClientError.code ?? runtime_error. Explicit ClientError.data !== undefined wins even null; otherwise conflict then computer invalid_argument recovery, else omitted data.',
  'Conflict classifier checks direct/error/response.error code and recognized message tokens then cycle-safe cause chain. Message suffix matching requires the token to be whole message or follow colon-space/newline; strip helper removes only trailing colon-space code. Four owner-conflict recovery variants distinguish target removed/no blind retry, owner changed/rerun, fencing/update host, and invalid destination/show current owner.',
  'Computer recovery switch has stable nextSteps for declared computer error codes, specialized screenshot/permission/window/app cases and delivered-key focus wording; unknown code returns undefined. A test iterating every known code proves only nonempty recovery coverage, not every conditional branch.',
